    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"alert-dialog-1\" description=\"An alert dialog with cancel and continue buttons.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Alert dialogs are the nuclear option of UI interruption. Unlike regular dialogs, they can't be dismissed by clicking outside or pressing Escape -- the user must explicitly choose an action. Reserve them for destructive operations where an accidental dismissal could mean data loss.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli@ add alert-dialog\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/primitives\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Make sure you have the <a href=\"/docs/components/dialog\"><code>Dialog</code></a> component installed in your project.</step></p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"alert-dialog\">\n<p><step>Add the <code>Dialog</code> component to your project.</step></p>\n<p>The <code>AlertDialog</code> component uses the <a href=\"/docs/components/dialog\"><code>Dialog</code></a> component. Make sure you have it installed in your project.</p>\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import {\n  AlertDialog,\n  AlertDialogAction,\n  AlertDialogCancel,\n  AlertDialogContent,\n  AlertDialogDescription,\n  AlertDialogFooter,\n  AlertDialogHeader,\n  AlertDialogTitle,\n  AlertDialogTrigger,\n} from '@/components/ui/alert-dialog';\nimport { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;AlertDialog>\n  &#x3C;AlertDialogTrigger>Open&#x3C;/AlertDialogTrigger>\n  &#x3C;AlertDialogContent>\n    &#x3C;AlertDialogHeader>\n      &#x3C;AlertDialogTitle>Are you absolutely sure?&#x3C;/AlertDialogTitle>\n      &#x3C;AlertDialogDescription>\n        This action cannot be undone. This will permanently delete your account and remove your data from our servers.\n      &#x3C;/AlertDialogDescription>\n    &#x3C;/AlertDialogHeader>\n    &#x3C;AlertDialogFooter>\n      &#x3C;AlertDialogCancel>Cancel&#x3C;/AlertDialogCancel>\n      &#x3C;AlertDialogAction>Continue&#x3C;/AlertDialogAction>\n    &#x3C;/AlertDialogFooter>\n  &#x3C;/AlertDialogContent>\n&#x3C;/AlertDialog>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[AlertDialog] --> B[AlertDialogTrigger]     A --> C[AlertDialogContent]     C --> D[AlertDialogHeader]     C --> E[AlertDialogFooter]     D --> F[AlertDialogTitle]     D --> G[AlertDialogDescription]     E --> H[AlertDialogAction]     E --> I[AlertDialogCancel] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>AlertDialog</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>defaultOpen</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Determines if the dialog should be open by default</td></tr><tr><td><code>open</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Controls the visibility of the dialog</td></tr><tr><td><code>onOpenChange</code></td><td><code>(open: boolean) => void</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Callback fired when the dialog opens or closes</td></tr><tr><td><code>closeButton</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether to render the close button inside the content</td></tr><tr><td><code>modal</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Whether the dialog is modal (locks interaction with the rest of the page)</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>Child elements (typically Trigger and Content)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>AlertDialogTrigger</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>asChild</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>If <code>true</code>, renders using a <code>Slot</code> instead of a <code>button</code> element</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Content of the trigger</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>button</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogCloseX</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>size</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>16</code></td><td>Size in pixels for the close icon</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>&#x3C;X /></code></td><td>Custom close icon; defaults to the <code>X</code> icon from lucide-react</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>button</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogContent</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Content displayed inside the dialog</td></tr><tr><td><code>forceMount</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>If <code>true</code>, forces the content to stay mounted in the DOM</td></tr><tr><td><code>renderOnce</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>If <code>true</code>, mounts content only once and preserves it</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard <code>AlertDialogPrimitive.Content</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogHeader</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Header content (typically Title and Description)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard <code>AlertDialogPrimitive.Heading</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogFooter</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Footer content (typically Action and Cancel buttons)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogTitle</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Title text content</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard <code>AlertDialogPrimitive.Title</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogDescription</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Description text content</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard <code>AlertDialogPrimitive.Description</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AlertDialogAction</h3>\n<p>Alias for <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code>. Accepts the same props.</p>\n<h3>AlertDialogCancel</h3>\n<p>Alias for <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code>. Accepts the same props.</p>",
