    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"avatar-1\" title=\"Avatar\" description=\"An avatar with a fallback.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Identity in UI starts with a face. Avatars humanize interfaces by giving users a visual anchor. We support both single avatars and groups because social context -- seeing who else is involved -- is a fundamental interaction pattern. The fallback-to-initials behavior ensures graceful degradation when images fail.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add avatar\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"avatar\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">import { Avatar, AvatarFallback, AvatarImage } from \"@/components/ui/avatar\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">&#x3C;Avatar src=\"https://github.com/wildduck2.png\" fallback=\"WD\" alt=\"wildduck\" />\n</code></pre>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Avatar</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>fallback</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Text displayed when the image fails to load; truncated to the first 2 characters</td></tr><tr><td><code>alt</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Alternate text for the avatar image, also used as <code>aria-label</code> on the fallback</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names for styling the avatar container</td></tr><tr><td><code>ref</code></td><td><code>React.Ref&#x3C;HTMLImageElement></code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Ref for the underlying <code>img</code> element</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>img</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>AvatarGroup</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>imgs</code></td><td><code>React.HTMLProps&#x3C;HTMLImageElement>[]</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>Array of props for each avatar image</td></tr><tr><td><code>maxVisible</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>3</code></td><td>Maximum number of avatars to display before showing overflow count</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names for styling the avatar group container</td></tr><tr><td><code>ref</code></td><td><code>React.Ref&#x3C;HTMLDivElement></code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Ref for the container element</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>",
