    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"button-group-1\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Individual buttons sometimes belong together. ButtonGroup handles the visual joining -- shared borders, connected radii, consistent spacing -- so you don't manually manage CSS for grouped actions. It's a layout primitive, not a logic primitive: each button inside still owns its own behavior.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD   ButtonGroup[ButtonGroup]   ButtonGroup --> variants[\"@gentleduck/variants\"]:::internal   ButtonGroup --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/slot\"]:::internal   ButtonGroup --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal   ButtonGroup --> Button[\"Button\"]:::component   ButtonGroup --> Separator[\"Separator\"]:::component   variants --> |\"provides\"| LayoutVariants[\"Layout Variants\\n(horizontal, vertical)\"]   primitives --> |\"provides\"| SlotRendering[\"Slot Rendering\"]   ButtonGroup --> |\"manages\"| ConnectedBorders[\"Connected Borders\\n&#x26; Radii\"]   classDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff   classDef component fill:#fb923c,stroke:#f97316,color:#fff </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add button-group\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/primitives\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"button-group\" title=\"components/ui/button-group.tsx\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import {\n  ButtonGroup,\n  ButtonGroupSeparator,\n  ButtonGroupText,\n} from \"@/components/ui/button-group\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;ButtonGroup>\n  &#x3C;Button>Button 1&#x3C;/Button>\n  &#x3C;Button>Button 2&#x3C;/Button>\n&#x3C;/ButtonGroup>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Accessibility</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>ButtonGroup</code> component has the <code>role</code> attribute set to <code>group</code>.</li>\n<li>Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to navigate between the buttons in the group.</li>\n<li>Use <code>aria-label</code> or <code>aria-labelledby</code> to label the button group.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">&#x3C;ButtonGroup aria-label=\"Button group\">\n  &#x3C;Button>Button 1&#x3C;/Button>\n  &#x3C;Button>Button 2&#x3C;/Button>\n&#x3C;/ButtonGroup>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>ButtonGroup vs ToggleGroup</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the <code>ButtonGroup</code> component when you want to group buttons that perform an action.</li>\n<li>Use the <code>ToggleGroup</code> component when you want to group buttons that toggle a state.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Orientation</h3>\n<p>Set the <code>orientation</code> prop to change the button group layout.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-2\">\n<h3>Size</h3>\n<p>Control the size of buttons using the <code>size</code> prop on individual buttons.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-3\">\n<h3>Nested</h3>\n<p>Nest <code>&#x3C;ButtonGroup></code> components to create button groups with spacing.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-4\">\n<h3>Separator</h3>\n<p>The <code>ButtonGroupSeparator</code> component visually divides buttons within a group.</p>\n<p>Buttons with variant <code>outline</code> do not need a separator since they have a border. For other variants, a separator is recommended to improve the visual hierarchy.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-5\">\n<h3>Split</h3>\n<p>Create a split button group by adding two buttons separated by a <code>ButtonGroupSeparator</code>.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-6\">\n<h3>Input</h3>\n<p>Wrap an <code>Input</code> component with buttons.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-7\">\n<h3>Input Group</h3>\n<p>Wrap an <code>InputGroup</code> component to create complex input layouts.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-8\">\n<h3>Dropdown Menu</h3>\n<p>Create a split button group with a <code>DropdownMenu</code> component.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-9\">\n<h3>Select</h3>\n<p>Pair with a <code>Select</code> component.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-10\">\n<h3>Popover</h3>\n<p>Use with a <code>Popover</code> component.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"button-group-11\">\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>ButtonGroup</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>orientation</code></td><td><code>'horizontal' | 'vertical'</code></td><td><code>'horizontal'</code></td><td>Layout direction of the button group</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Grouped content (buttons, separators, text, or nested groups)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>ButtonGroupSeparator</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>orientation</code></td><td><code>'horizontal' | 'vertical'</code></td><td><code>'vertical'</code></td><td>Orientation of the separator line</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard <code>Separator</code> component props.</em></p>\n<h3>ButtonGroupText</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>asChild</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>If <code>true</code>, uses the <code>Slot</code> component instead of rendering a <code>div</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Text content to display</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview>",
    "description": "A container that groups related button like elements together with consistent styling.",
