    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"command-1\" align=\"start\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview>div]:max-w-[450px]\" description=\"A command menu\" showsettings=\"{false}\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Searchable Command Dialog:</strong> Command palette with fuzzy search and real-time filtering.</li>\n<li><strong>Groupable Command List:</strong> Organize commands into logical groups with optional headings.</li>\n<li><strong>Selectable Items:</strong> Items support click actions, selection states, and checkmark indicators.</li>\n<li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> Full keyboard support with arrow keys, Enter, and Escape navigation.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom Shortcuts:</strong> Optional shortcut labels shown beside each command item.</li>\n<li><strong>Empty State Handling:</strong> Automatically displays a fallback when no items match the query.</li>\n<li><strong>Loopable Navigation:</strong> Optional looping behavior for continuous up/down key cycling.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom Filtering Logic:</strong> Swap out the built-in filter with your own function.</li>\n<li><strong>Accessible &#x26; Composable:</strong> ARIA roles and headless architecture for complete flexibility.</li>\n<li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Adapts gracefully to different screen sizes and containers.</li>\n<li><strong>Dialog or Inline Support:</strong> Can be used as a floating dialog or embedded inline.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>About</h2>\n<p>This component uses the <a href=\"https://github.com/gentleeduck/ui/tree/master/packages/duck-vim\">@gentleduck/vim</a> library under the hood.</p>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Command palettes are the power user's best friend -- they surface every action in the app behind a single keyboard shortcut. We wrap cmdk because it handles fuzzy search, group filtering, and keyboard navigation with minimal API surface. The composable sub-components let you build anything from a simple search to a full IDE-style command center.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={`graph TD\nCommand[Command]\nCommand --> vim[\"@gentleduck/vim\"]:::internal\nCommand --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal\nCommand --> Dialog[\"Dialog\"]:::component\nCommand --> ScrollArea[\"ScrollArea\"]:::component\nCommand --> lucide[\"lucide-react\"]:::external</p>\n<p>vim --> |\"provides\"| KeyBindings[\"Key Bindings Registry\"]\nCommand --> |\"custom\"| Hooks[\"useCommandSearch\\nuseHandleKeyDown\"]\nCommand --> |\"custom\"| SelectionLogic[\"Item Selection &#x26;\\nFiltering Logic\"]\nCommand --> |\"uses\"| Context[\"React Context\\n(Refs + State)\"]</p>\n<p>classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff\nclassDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff\nclassDef component fill:#fb923c,stroke:#f97316,color:#fff\n`} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add command\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/vim @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Add the <code>Dialog</code> and <code>ScrollArea</code> components to your project.</step></p>\n<p>The <code>Command</code> component uses the <a href=\"/components/dialog\"><code>Dialog</code></a> and <a href=\"/components/scroll-area\"><code>ScrollArea</code></a> component. Make sure you have it installed in your project.</p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"command\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import {\n  Command,\n  CommandDialog,\n  CommandEmpty,\n  CommandGroup,\n  CommandInput,\n  CommandItem,\n  CommandList,\n  CommandSeparator,\n  CommandShortcut,\n} from '@/components/ui'\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Command>\n  &#x3C;CommandInput placeholder=\"Type a command or search...\" />\n  &#x3C;CommandList>\n    &#x3C;CommandEmpty>No results found.&#x3C;/CommandEmpty>\n    &#x3C;CommandGroup heading=\"Suggestions\">\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>Search GitHub&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>Search Twitter&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>Search Discord&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n    &#x3C;/CommandGroup>\n    &#x3C;CommandSeparator />\n    &#x3C;CommandGroup heading=\"Settings\">\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>General&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>Profile&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n      &#x3C;CommandItem>Notifications&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n    &#x3C;/CommandGroup>\n  &#x3C;/CommandList>\n&#x3C;/Command>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Dialog</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"command-2\" description=\"A component dialog.\" showsettings=\"{false}\"></componentpreview></p>\n<p>To show the command menu in a dialog, use the <code>&#x3C;CommandDialog /></code> component, or use the <code>&#x3C;Button/></code> component with the <code>command</code> variant.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { useKeyCommands } from '@gentleduck/vim/react'\n\nexport function CommandMenu() {\n  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false)\n\n  useKeyCommands({\n    'ctrl+j': {\n      name: '⌘j',\n      description: 'Open command menu',\n      execute: () => {\n        window.event?.preventDefault()\n        setOpen(true)\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n\n  return (\n    &#x3C;CommandDialog\n      open={open}\n      onOpenChange={setOpen}\n    >\n      &#x3C;CommandInput placeholder=\"Type a command or search...\" />\n      &#x3C;CommandList>\n        &#x3C;CommandEmpty>No results found.&#x3C;/CommandEmpty>\n        &#x3C;CommandGroup heading=\"Suggestions\">\n          &#x3C;CommandItem>Settings&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n          &#x3C;CommandItem>Messages&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n          &#x3C;CommandItem>Search&#x3C;/CommandItem>\n        &#x3C;/CommandGroup>\n      &#x3C;/CommandList>\n    &#x3C;/CommandDialog>\n  )\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[Command] --> B[CommandInput]     A --> C[CommandList]     C --> D[CommandEmpty]     C --> E[CommandGroup]     C --> F[CommandSeparator]     E --> G[CommandItem]     G --> H[CommandShortcut]     A -.->|dialog mode| I[CommandDialog]     I --> A </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Command</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS classes applied to the command container</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Command content (<code>CommandInput</code>, <code>CommandList</code>, etc.)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandInput</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>'Search...'</code></td><td>Placeholder text in the input</td></tr><tr><td><code>autoFocus</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Automatically focus input on mount</td></tr><tr><td><code>onChange</code></td><td><code>React.ChangeEventHandler</code></td><td>--</td><td>Triggered when the input value changes</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>input</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandList</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS classes applied to the list</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td><code>CommandGroup</code>, <code>CommandItem</code>, <code>CommandEmpty</code>, and <code>CommandSeparator</code> elements</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>ul</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandItem</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>The internal value for selection</td></tr><tr><td><code>onSelect</code></td><td><code>(value: string) => void</code></td><td>--</td><td>Called when the item is selected</td></tr><tr><td><code>onClick</code></td><td><code>React.MouseEventHandler</code></td><td>--</td><td>Native click event</td></tr><tr><td><code>onKeyDown</code></td><td><code>React.KeyboardEventHandler</code></td><td>--</td><td>Native keydown event</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>li</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandGroup</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>heading</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Optional heading for the group</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandEmpty</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS classes applied to the empty state</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Content shown when no items match the search query</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>h6</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandShortcut</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>keys</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Keyboard shortcut string (e.g. <code>\"ctrl+K\"</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>onKeysPressed</code></td><td><code>() => void</code></td><td>--</td><td>Triggered when shortcut is pressed</td></tr><tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td><code>'default' | 'secondary'</code></td><td><code>'default'</code></td><td>Visual style variant</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>kbd</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandSeparator</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS classes applied to the separator</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>CommandDialog</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Command content rendered inside the dialog (typically <code>CommandInput</code>, <code>CommandList</code>, etc.)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>Dialog</code> props (<code>open</code>, <code>onOpenChange</code>, <code>closeButton</code>, etc.).</em></p>\n<h2>Types</h2>\n<h3><strong>CommandContextType</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>search</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>Current search query value.</td></tr><tr><td><code>setSearch</code></td><td><code>React.Dispatch&#x3C;React.SetStateAction&#x3C;string>></code></td><td>Setter for search query.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>CommandRefsContextType</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>commandRef</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLDivElement | null></code></td><td>Root command container reference.</td></tr><tr><td><code>listRef</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLUListElement | null></code></td><td>UL element holding items.</td></tr><tr><td><code>emptyRef</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLHeadingElement | null></code></td><td>Empty state heading ref.</td></tr><tr><td><code>inputRef</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLInputElement | null></code></td><td>Search input field reference.</td></tr><tr><td><code>selectedItem</code></td><td><code>HTMLLIElement | null</code></td><td>Currently selected item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>setSelectedItem</code></td><td><code>React.Dispatch&#x3C;React.SetStateAction&#x3C;HTMLLIElement | null>></code></td><td>Setter for selected item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>items</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLLIElement[]></code></td><td>All command items.</td></tr><tr><td><code>filteredItems</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLLIElement[]></code></td><td>Filtered items after search.</td></tr><tr><td><code>groups</code></td><td><code>React.RefObject&#x3C;HTMLDivElement[]></code></td><td>Groups of command items.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>CommandBadgeProps (CommandShortcut)</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>keys</code></td><t