    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"empty-1\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-0\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Empty states are opportunities, not dead ends. When there's no data to show, the Empty component turns a blank screen into a call to action. We structure it as header + content because every empty state needs two things: an explanation of why it's empty, and a path forward. The media slot (icon, avatar, illustration) adds emotional tone.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD   Empty[Empty]   Empty --> variants[\"@gentleduck/variants\"]:::internal   Empty --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal   variants --> |\"provides\"| VariantSystem[\"Layout Variants\"]   Empty --> |\"composes\"| EmptyHeader[\"EmptyHeader\"]   Empty --> |\"composes\"| EmptyContent[\"EmptyContent\"]   EmptyHeader --> EmptyMedia[\"EmptyMedia\\n(icon/avatar/image)\"]   EmptyHeader --> EmptyTitle[\"EmptyTitle\"]   EmptyHeader --> EmptyDescription[\"EmptyDescription\"]   classDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add empty\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/libs @gentleduck/variants\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"empty\" title=\"components/ui/empty.tsx\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import {\n  Empty,\n  EmptyContent,\n  EmptyDescription,\n  EmptyHeader,\n  EmptyMedia,\n  EmptyTitle,\n} from \"@/components/ui/empty\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Empty>\n  &#x3C;EmptyHeader>\n    &#x3C;EmptyMedia variant=\"icon\">\n      &#x3C;Icon />\n    &#x3C;/EmptyMedia>\n  &#x3C;/EmptyHeader>\n  &#x3C;EmptyTitle>No data&#x3C;/EmptyTitle>\n  &#x3C;EmptyDescription>No data found&#x3C;/EmptyDescription>\n  &#x3C;EmptyContent>\n    &#x3C;Button>Add data&#x3C;/Button>\n  &#x3C;/EmptyContent>\n&#x3C;/Empty>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Outline</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>border</code> utility class to create a outline empty state.</p>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"empty-2\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-6 md:[&#x26;_.preview]:p-10\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>Background</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>bg-*</code> and <code>bg-gradient-*</code> utilities to add a background to the empty state.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"empty-3\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-0\">\n<h3>Avatar</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyMedia</code> component to display an avatar in the empty state.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"empty-4\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-0\">\n<h3>Avatar Group</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyMedia</code> component to display an avatar group in the empty state.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"empty-5\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-0\">\n<h3>InputGroup</h3>\n<p>You can add an <code>InputGroup</code> component to the <code>EmptyContent</code> component.</p>\n<componentpreview name=\"empty-6\" class=\"[&#x26;_.preview]:p-0\">\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[Empty] --> B[EmptyHeader]     B --> C[EmptyMedia]     A --> D[EmptyTitle]     A --> E[EmptyDescription]     A --> F[EmptyContent] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Empty</h3>\n<p>The main component of the empty state. Wraps the <code>EmptyHeader</code> and <code>EmptyContent</code> components.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Empty state content</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>EmptyHeader</h3>\n<p>The <code>EmptyHeader</code> component wraps the empty media, title, and description.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Header content (media, title, description)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>EmptyMedia</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyMedia</code> component to display the media of the empty state such as an icon or an image. You can also use it to display other components such as an avatar.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td><code>'default' | 'icon'</code></td><td><code>'default'</code></td><td>Visual variant of the media container</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Media content (icon, avatar, image)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>EmptyTitle</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyTitle</code> component to display the title of the empty state.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Title text</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>EmptyDescription</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyDescription</code> component to display the description of the empty state.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Description text</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>p</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>EmptyContent</h3>\n<p>Use the <code>EmptyContent</code> component to display the content of the empty state such as a button, input or a link.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Action content (buttons, links, inputs)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview></componentpreview>",
