    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"hover-card-1\" description=\"A hover card component\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Hover cards provide progressive disclosure without commitment. They let users preview content before clicking, reducing unnecessary navigation. We build on Popover primitives because hover cards are fundamentally popovers with mouse-enter triggers -- shared internals mean consistent behavior and smaller bundle size.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD   HoverCard[HoverCard]   HoverCard --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/hover-card\"]:::internal   HoverCard --> motion[\"@gentleduck/motion\"]:::internal   HoverCard --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal   HoverCard --> Button[\"Button\"]:::component   primitives --> |\"provides\"| HoverTrigger[\"Hover Detection\\n&#x26; Timing\"]   primitives --> |\"provides\"| Positioning[\"Floating UI\\nPositioning\"]   motion --> |\"provides\"| AnimVariants[\"Entry/Exit\\nAnimations\"]   classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff   classDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff   classDef component fill:#fb923c,stroke:#f97316,color:#fff </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add hover-card\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/primitives @gentleduck/libs @gentleduck/motion @gentleduck/variants  \n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Add the <code>Button</code> component to your project.</step></p>\n<p>The <code>HoverCard</code> component uses the <a href=\"/components/button\"><code>Button</code></a> component. Make sure you have it installed in your project.</p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"hover-card\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import {\n  HoverCard,\n  HoverCardContent,\n  HoverCardTrigger,\n} from \"@/components/ui/hover-card\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;HoverCard>\n  &#x3C;HoverCardTrigger>Hover&#x3C;/HoverCardTrigger>\n  &#x3C;HoverCardContent>\n    The React Framework – created and maintained by @vercel.\n  &#x3C;/HoverCardContent>\n&#x3C;/HoverCard>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>HoverCard</h3>\n<p>Root wrapper that provides hover-card state and context. Wraps <code>HoverCardPrimitive.Root</code> internally.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>placement</code></td><td><code>Placement</code></td><td><code>'top'</code></td><td>Position of the hover card relative to the trigger</td></tr><tr><td><code>skipDelayDuration</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Time in milliseconds to skip the delay when rapidly moving between triggers</td></tr><tr><td><code>delayDuration</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Delay time in milliseconds before showing the card</td></tr><tr><td><code>open</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Controlled open state</td></tr><tr><td><code>onOpenChange</code></td><td><code>(open: boolean) => void</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Callback when open state changes</td></tr><tr><td><code>defaultOpen</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Initial open state for uncontrolled usage</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>HoverCard sub-components</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>HoverCardPrimitive.Root</code> props (<code>sideOffset</code>, <code>alignOffset</code>, <code>mainAxis</code>, <code>modal</code>).</em></p>\n<h3>HoverCardTrigger</h3>\n<p>The element that triggers the hover card on hover. Renders a <code>Button</code> internally.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>'outline'</code></td><td>Variant style applied to the internal <code>Button</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>asChild</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Whether to use the child as the trigger element directly</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Content rendered inside the trigger button</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>HoverCardPrimitive.Trigger</code> and <code>Button</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>HoverCardContent</h3>\n<p>The content displayed when the hover card is open. Wraps <code>HoverCardPrimitive.Content</code> with animation and styling.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes to apply to the content container</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Content rendered inside the hover card</td></tr><tr><td><code>forceMount</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Keep content mounted for CSS-driven animations</td></tr><tr><td><code>renderOnce</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Keep content mounted after first open</td></tr><tr><td><code>lockScroll</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Locks page scroll while the hover card is open</td></tr><tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Disables focus management when true</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>HoverCardPrimitive.Content</code> props and standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p></componentpreview>",
    "description": "For sighted users to preview content available behind a link.",
    "excerpt": "\nPhilosophy\nHover cards provide progressive disclosure without commitment. They let users preview content before clicking, reducing unnecessary navigation. We build on Popover primitives because hover cards are fundamentally popovers with mouse-enter triggers ",
