    "component": true,
    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"label-1\" description=\"A label\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Labels are the accessibility backbone of every form. A form control without a label is invisible to screen readers. We ship Label as a standalone component rather than baking it into every form element because composition is more flexible than configuration -- you decide where the label goes and how it connects.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add label\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"label\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Label } from \"@/components/ui/label\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Label htmlFor=\"email\">Your email address&#x3C;/Label>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Label</h3>\n<p>Renders an accessible label element associated with form controls.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional class names for the label element</td></tr><tr><td><code>htmlFor</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>The <code>id</code> of the form element this label is associated with</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Label text or elements</td></tr><tr><td><code>ref</code></td><td><code>React.Ref&#x3C;HTMLLabelElement></code></td><td>--</td><td>Ref forwarded to the label element</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>label</code> props.</em></p></componentpreview>",
