    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"navigation-menu-1\" class=\"[&#x26;_&#x26;[duck-preview]]:overflow-visible\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Navigation menus serve a different purpose than dropdown menus -- they're for wayfinding, not actions. The distinction matters for accessibility: navigation menus use <code>&#x3C;nav></code> and link semantics, while dropdown menus use <code>role=\"menu\"</code> and button semantics. We expose viewport and indicator sub-components for advanced hover/focus animations.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add navigation-menu\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @radix-ui/react-navigation-menu @gentleduck/libs @gentleduck/variants\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<p><componentsource name=\"navigation-menu\" title=\"components/ui/navigation-menu.tsx\"></componentsource></p>\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">import {\n  NavigationMenu,\n  NavigationMenuContent,\n  NavigationMenuIndicator,\n  NavigationMenuItem,\n  NavigationMenuLink,\n  NavigationMenuList,\n  NavigationMenuTrigger,\n  NavigationMenuViewport,\n} from \"@/components/ui/navigation-menu\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">&#x3C;NavigationMenu>\n  &#x3C;NavigationMenuList>\n    &#x3C;NavigationMenuItem>\n      &#x3C;NavigationMenuTrigger>Item One&#x3C;/NavigationMenuTrigger>\n      &#x3C;NavigationMenuContent>\n        &#x3C;NavigationMenuLink>Link&#x3C;/NavigationMenuLink>\n      &#x3C;/NavigationMenuContent>\n    &#x3C;/NavigationMenuItem>\n  &#x3C;/NavigationMenuList>\n&#x3C;/NavigationMenu>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[NavigationMenu] --> B[NavigationMenuList]     B --> C[NavigationMenuItem]     C --> D[NavigationMenuTrigger]     C --> E[NavigationMenuContent]     C --> F[NavigationMenuLink]     A --> G[NavigationMenuViewport]     A --> H[NavigationMenuIndicator] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Link</h2>\n<p>You can use the <code>asChild</code> prop to make another component look like a navigation menu trigger. Here's an example of a link that looks like a navigation menu trigger.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers title=&#x22;components/example-navigation-menu.tsx&#x22;\">import { Link } from \"next/link\"\n\nexport function NavigationMenuDemo() {\n  return (\n    &#x3C;NavigationMenuItem>\n      &#x3C;NavigationMenuLink asChild>\n        &#x3C;Link href=\"/docs\">Documentation&#x3C;/Link>\n      &#x3C;/NavigationMenuLink>\n    &#x3C;/NavigationMenuItem>\n  )\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>NavigationMenu</h3>\n<p>Root container that wraps the navigation menu and optionally renders the viewport.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>viewport</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether to render the <code>NavigationMenuViewport</code> automatically</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the root element</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Navigation menu list and other elements</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Root</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuList</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the list element</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.List</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuItem</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the menu item</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Item</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuTrigger</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the trigger</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Trigger label content. A chevron icon is appended automatically</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Trigger</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuContent</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the content panel</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Content</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuLink</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the link</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Link</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuViewport</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the viewport</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Viewport</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>NavigationMenuIndicator</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the indicator</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>NavigationMenuPrimitive.Indicator</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>navigationMenuTriggerStyle</h3>\n<p>A <code>cva</code> variant function that returns the default trigger styling classes. Use it to style non-trigger elements (e.g. plain links) to match the trigger appearance.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { navigationMenuTriggerStyle } from \"@/components/ui/navigation-menu\"\n\n&#x3C;NavigationMenuLink className={navigationMenuTriggerStyle()}>\n  Documentation\n&#x3C;/NavigationMenuLink>\n</code></pre></componentpreview>",
