    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"radio-group-1\" description=\"A radio group with 3 items.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Radio groups enforce single selection from a set -- the constraint is the feature. Unlike checkboxes (multi-select) or selects (dropdown), radio groups make all options visible simultaneously. We use native radio inputs for built-in keyboard navigation (arrow keys cycle through options) and form integration.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={`graph TD\nRadioGroup[RadioGroup]\nRadioGroup --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/checkers\"]:::internal\nRadioGroup --> motion[\"@gentleduck/motion\"]:::internal\nRadioGroup --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal</p>\n<p>primitives --> |\"provides\"| SvgIndicator[\"useSvgIndicator\\n(dot indicator)\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| NativeRadio[\"Native Radio\\nInputs\"]\nmotion --> |\"provides\"| AnimVariants[\"Selection\\nAnimation\"]\nRadioGroup --> |\"adds\"| ArrowNav[\"Arrow Key\\nNavigation\"]\nRadioGroup --> |\"adds\"| GroupContext[\"RadioGroup\\nContext\"]</p>\n<p>classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff\nclassDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff\n`} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add radio-group\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/primitives @gentleduck/motion @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Add the <code>Label</code> component to your project.</step></p>\n<p>The <code>RadioGroup</code> component uses the <a href=\"/components/label\"><code>Label</code></a> component. Make sure you have it installed in your project.</p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"radio-group\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Label } from \"@/components/ui/label\"\nimport { RadioGroup, RadioGroupItem } from \"@/components/ui/radio-group\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;RadioGroup defaultValue=\"option-one\">\n  &#x3C;div className=\"flex items-center space-x-2\">\n    &#x3C;RadioGroupItem value=\"option-one\" id=\"option-one\" />\n    &#x3C;Label htmlFor=\"option-one\">Option One&#x3C;/Label>\n  &#x3C;/div>\n  &#x3C;div className=\"flex items-center space-x-2\">\n    &#x3C;RadioGroupItem value=\"option-two\" id=\"option-two\" />\n    &#x3C;Label htmlFor=\"option-two\">Option Two&#x3C;/Label>\n  &#x3C;/div>\n&#x3C;/RadioGroup>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<componentpreview name=\"radio-group-2\">\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[RadioGroup] --> B[RadioGroupItem]     B --> C[Radio]     B --> D[Label]     C --> E[Hidden Input]     C --> F[SVG Indicator] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>RadioGroup</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Controlled value of the selected radio item</td></tr><tr><td><code>defaultValue</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Initial selected value when uncontrolled</td></tr><tr><td><code>onValueChange</code></td><td><code>(value: string) => void</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Callback fired when selection changes</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the radio group list</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td><code>RadioGroupItem</code> elements</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>ul</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>RadioGroupItem</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>Unique value for the radio item, also used as the element's <code>id</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>customIndicator</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Custom indicator element rendered inside the item</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the list item</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Label content rendered via the <code>Label</code> component</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>li</code> props (except <code>value</code>).</em></p>\n<h3>Radio</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>indicator</code></td><td><code>React.ReactElement</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Custom SVG or element for unchecked state indicator</td></tr><tr><td><code>checkedIndicator</code></td><td><code>React.ReactElement</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Custom SVG or element for checked state indicator</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>input</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>useRadioGroupContext</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hook to consume the <code>RadioGroupContext</code>.</li>\n<li>Throws an error if used outside of a <code>RadioGroup</code> provider.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>useHandleRadioClick</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hook to manage click handlers and ARIA states on radio items.</li>\n<li>Accepts optional <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>value</code>, and <code>onValueChange</code> callback.</li>\n<li>Returns refs to the wrapper (<code>&#x3C;ul></code>), selected item, and all items.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>See also</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/checkbox\">Checkbox</a> -- Multi-selection toggle control</li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/switch\">Switch</a> -- Toggle between on and off states</li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/select\">Select</a> -- Dropdown selection from a list</li>\n</ul></componentpreview>",
