    "content": "<p>Forms are tricky. They are one of the most common things you'll build in a web application, but also one of the most complex.</p>\n<p>Well-designed HTML forms are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Well-structured and semantically correct.</li>\n<li>Easy to use and navigate (keyboard).</li>\n<li>Accessible with ARIA attributes and proper labels.</li>\n<li>Has support for client and server side validation.</li>\n<li>Well-styled and consistent with the rest of the application.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In this guide, we will take a look at building forms with <a href=\"https://react-hook-form.com/\"><code>react-hook-form</code></a> and <a href=\"https://zod.dev\"><code>zod</code></a>. We're going to use a <code>&#x3C;FormField></code> component to compose accessible forms using Radix UI components.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<p>The <code>&#x3C;Form /></code> component is a wrapper around the <code>react-hook-form</code> library. It provides a few things:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Composable components for building forms.</li>\n<li>A <code>&#x3C;FormField /></code> component for building controlled form fields.</li>\n<li>Form validation using <code>zod</code>.</li>\n<li>Handles accessibility and error messages.</li>\n<li>Uses <code>React.useId()</code> for generating unique IDs.</li>\n<li>Applies the correct <code>aria</code> attributes to form fields based on states.</li>\n<li>Built to work with all Radix UI components.</li>\n<li>Bring your own schema library. We use <code>zod</code> but you can use anything you want.</li>\n<li><strong>You have full control over the markup and styling.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Form validation shouldn't require a PhD. We integrate with React Hook Form because it validates at the field level without re-rendering the entire form. The Form/FormField/FormItem/FormControl pattern maps directly to how forms work: each field has a label, an input, a description, and an error message.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={`graph TD\nForm[Form]\nForm --> rhf[\"react-hook-form\"]:::external\nForm --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/slot\"]:::internal\nForm --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal\nForm --> Label[\"Label\"]:::component</p>\n<p>rhf --> |\"provides\"| Validation[\"Field Validation\"]\nrhf --> |\"provides\"| FormState[\"Form State\\nManagement\"]\nrhf --> |\"provides\"| Controller[\"Controlled\\nInputs\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| Slot[\"Slot Rendering\\n(asChild)\"]\nForm --> |\"adds\"| FieldContext[\"Field-level\\nReact Context\"]\nForm --> |\"adds\"| ErrorDisplay[\"Error Message\\nComponents\"]</p>\n<p>classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff\nclassDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff\nclassDef component fill:#fb923c,stroke:#f97316,color:#fff\n`} /></p>\n<h2>Anatomy</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">&#x3C;Form>\n  &#x3C;FormField\n    control={...}\n    name=\"...\"\n    render={() => (\n      &#x3C;FormItem>\n        &#x3C;FormLabel />\n        &#x3C;FormControl>\n          { /* Your form field */}\n        &#x3C;/FormControl>\n        &#x3C;FormDescription />\n        &#x3C;FormMessage />\n      &#x3C;/FormItem>\n    )}\n  />\n&#x3C;/Form>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Example</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers\">const form = useForm()\n\n&#x3C;FormField\n  control={form.control}\n  name=\"username\"\n  render={({ field }) => (\n    &#x3C;FormItem>\n      &#x3C;FormLabel>Username&#x3C;/FormLabel>\n      &#x3C;FormControl>\n        &#x3C;Input placeholder=\"wildduck\" {...field} />\n      &#x3C;/FormControl>\n      &#x3C;FormDescription>This is your public display name.&#x3C;/FormDescription>\n      &#x3C;FormMessage />\n    &#x3C;/FormItem>\n  )}\n/>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add form\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install react-hook-form @hookform/resolvers zod @gentleduck/primitives @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Make sure you have the <a href=\"/docs/components/label\"><code>Label</code></a> component installed in your project.</step></p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"react-hook-form\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<steps>\n<p><step>Create a form schema</step></p>\n<p>Define the shape of your form using a Zod schema. You can read more about using Zod in the <a href=\"https://zod.dev\">Zod documentation</a>.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers {3,5-7}\">\"use client\"\n\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  username: z.string().min(2).max(50),\n})\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Define a form</step></p>\n<p>Use the <code>useForm</code> hook from <code>react-hook-form</code> to create a form.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers {3-4,14-20,22-27}\">\"use client\"\n\nimport { zodResolver } from \"@hookform/resolvers/zod\"\nimport { useForm } from \"react-hook-form\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  username: z.string().min(2, {\n    message: \"Username must be at least 2 characters.\",\n  }),\n})\n\nexport function ProfileForm() {\n  // 1. Define your form.\n  const form = useForm&#x3C;z.infer&#x3C;typeof formSchema>>({\n    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),\n    defaultValues: {\n      username: \"\",\n    },\n  })\n\n  // 2. Define a submit handler.\n  function onSubmit(values: z.infer&#x3C;typeof formSchema>) {\n    // Do something with the form values.\n    // ✅ This will be type-safe and validated.\n    console.log(values)\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Since <code>FormField</code> is using a controlled component, you need to provide a default value for the field. See the <a href=\"https://react-hook-form.com/docs/usecontroller\">React Hook Form docs</a> to learn more about controlled components.</p>\n<p><step>Build your form</step></p>\n<p>We can now use the <code>&#x3C;Form /></code> components to build our form.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\" metastring=\"showLineNumbers {7-17,28-50}\">\"use client\"\n\nimport { zodResolver } from \"@hookform/resolvers/zod\"\nimport { useForm } from \"react-hook-form\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Form,\n  FormControl,\n  FormDescription,\n  FormField,\n  FormItem,\n  FormLabel,\n  FormMessage,\n} from \"@/components/ui/form\"\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"\n\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  username: z.string().min(2, {\n    message: \"Username must be at least 2 characters.\",\n  }),\n})\n\nexport function ProfileForm() {\n  // ...\n\n  return (\n    &#x3C;Form {...form}>\n      &#x3C;form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-8\">\n        &#x3C;FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"username\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            &#x3C;FormItem>\n              &#x3C;FormLabel>Username&#x3C;/FormLabel>\n              &#x3C;FormControl>\n                &#x3C;Input placeholder=\"wildduck\" {...field} />\n              &#x3C;/FormControl>\n              &#x3C;FormDescription>\n                This is your public display name.\n              &#x3C;/FormDescription>\n              &#x3C;FormMessage />\n            &#x3C;/FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n        &#x3C;Button type=\"submit\">Submit&#x3C;/Button>\n      &#x3C;/form>\n    &#x3C;/Form>\n  )\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Done</step></p>\n<p>That's it. You now have a fully accessible form that is type-safe with client-side validation.</p>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"input-7\" class=\"[&#x26;_[role=tablist]]:hidden [&#x26;>div>div:first-child]:hidden\"></componentpreview></p>\n</steps>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<p>See the following links for more examples on how to use the <code>&#x3C;Form /></code> component with other components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/checkbox#form\">Checkbox</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/date-picker#form\">Date Picker</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/input#form\">Input</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/radio-group#form\">Radio Group</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/select#form\">Select</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/switch#form\">Switch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/textarea#form\">Textarea</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/components/combobox#form\">Combobox</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[Form] --> B[FormField]     B --> C[FormItem]     C --> D[FormLabel]     C --> E[FormControl]     C --> F[FormDescription]     C --> G[FormMessage] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<p><em>Accepts all <code>FormProviderProps</code> from <code>react-hook-form</code>.</em></p>\n<h3>FormField</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>name</code></td><td><code>FieldPath&#x3C;TFieldValues></code></td><td>(required)</td><td>The field name in your form schema</td></tr><tr><td><code>control</code></td><td><code>Control&#x3C;TFieldValues></code></td><td>(required)</td><td>The control object from <code>useForm</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>render</code></td><td><code>ControllerProps&#x3C;TFieldValues, TName>['render']</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>Render function receiving <code>{ field, fieldState, formState }</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>Controller</code> props from <code>react-hook-form</code>.</em></p>\n<h3>FormItem</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the form item wrapper</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Label, control, description, and message elements</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>FormLabel</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the label</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>Label</code> component props. Automatically receives <code>htmlFor</code> and <code>data-error</code> from form context.</em></p>\n<h3>FormControl</h3>\n<p>Renders its child via <code>Slot</code>, injecting <code>id</code>, <code>aria-describedby</code>, and <code>aria-invalid</code> from the form field context.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>The form control element (input, select, etc.)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>Slot</code> component props.</em></p>\n<h3>FormDescription</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the description text</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Help text content</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>p</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>FormMessage</h3>\n<p>Displays the field's validation error message. If no error exists, renders <code>children</code> or nothing.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Additional CSS classes for the message text</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td><code>--</code></td><td>Fallback content when no error is present</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>p</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>useFormField</h3>\n<p>Returns an object containing:</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>Internal form item ID</td></tr><tr><td><code>name</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>Field name</td></tr><tr><td><code>formItemId</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>ID for the form control</td></tr><tr><td><code>formDescriptionId</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>ID for the description</td></tr><tr><td><code>formMessageId</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>ID for the message</td></tr><tr><td><code>error</code></td><td><code>FieldError | undefined</code></td><td>Validation error object</td></tr></tbody></table>",
