    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"skeleton-1\" description=\"A skeleton component.\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Loading states deserve the same design attention as loaded states. Skeleton placeholders reduce perceived wait time by hinting at the shape of incoming content. We keep this component prop-less intentionally -- you control the shape through <code>className</code> and layout, mirroring the actual content it replaces.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add skeleton\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/libs \n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"skeleton\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Skeleton } from \"@/components/ui/skeleton\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Skeleton className=\"w-[100px] h-[20px] rounded-full\" />\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Card</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"skeleton-2\" description=\"A card with skeleton showing a loading state.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Skeleton</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names to control shape and size</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p></componentpreview>",
