    "content": "<componentpreview name=\"slider-1\" description=\"A slider component.\">\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Sliders let users select values within a range through direct manipulation. We build on Radix's accessible foundation (keyboard arrows, ARIA attributes, RTL support) and add the visual track/range/thumb styling. The Root/Track/Range/Thumb decomposition lets you restyle any part without rebuilding the interaction logic.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={`graph TD\nSlider[Slider]\nSlider --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/slider\"]:::internal\nSlider --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal</p>\n<p>primitives --> |\"provides\"| DragInteraction[\"Drag Interaction\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| KeyboardNav[\"Arrow Key Steps\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| A11y[\"ARIA slider\\nAttributes\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| RTL[\"RTL Support\"]\nSlider --> |\"adds\"| TrackStyle[\"Styled Track\\n&#x26; Range\"]\nSlider --> |\"adds\"| ThumbStyle[\"Styled Thumb\"]</p>\n<p>classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff\nclassDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff\n`} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add slider\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/libs @gentleduck/primitives\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"slider\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Slider } from \"@/components/ui/slider\"\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Slider defaultValue={[33]} max={100} step={1} />\n</code></pre>\n<componentpreview name=\"slider-2\" description=\"A slider component.\">\n<h2>Component Composition</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[Slider.Root] --> B[Slider.Track]     B --> C[Slider.Range]     A --> D[Slider.Thumb] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Slider</h3>\n<p>A single-thumb slider. Internally composes <code>SliderPrimitive.Root</code>, <code>SliderPrimitive.Track</code>, <code>SliderPrimitive.Range</code>, and <code>SliderPrimitive.Thumb</code>.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>SliderPrimitive.Root</code> props (including <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>step</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onValueChange</code>, <code>orientation</code>, <code>rtl</code>).</em></p>\n<h3>SliderRange</h3>\n<p>A dual-thumb range slider. Internally composes <code>SliderPrimitive.Root</code>, <code>SliderPrimitive.Track</code>, <code>SliderPrimitive.Range</code>, and two <code>SliderPrimitive.Thumb</code> elements (index 0 and 1).</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>SliderPrimitive.Root</code> props (including <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>step</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onValueChange</code>, <code>orientation</code>, <code>rtl</code>).</em></p>\n<h3>Primitive Sub-components</h3>\n<p>The following primitives are used internally by <code>Slider</code> and <code>SliderRange</code>:</p>\n<h4>SliderPrimitive.Root</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>min</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Minimum allowed value</td></tr><tr><td><code>max</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>100</code></td><td>Maximum allowed value</td></tr><tr><td><code>step</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Increment step for values</td></tr><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>number[]</code></td><td>--</td><td>Controlled values array (one or two values for range sliders)</td></tr><tr><td><code>defaultValue</code></td><td><code>number[]</code></td><td><code>[50]</code></td><td>Uncontrolled initial values</td></tr><tr><td><code>onValueChange</code></td><td><code>(value: number[]) => void</code></td><td>--</td><td>Callback fired when slider values change</td></tr><tr><td><code>orientation</code></td><td><code>'horizontal' | 'vertical'</code></td><td><code>'horizontal'</code></td><td>Slider orientation</td></tr><tr><td><code>rtl</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Enables right-to-left layout support</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props (except <code>defaultValue</code>).</em></p>\n<h4>SliderPrimitive.Track</h4>\n<p><em>Accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h4>SliderPrimitive.Range</h4>\n<p><em>Accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h4>SliderPrimitive.Thumb</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>index</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>The index of the thumb in the <code>values</code> array</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props.</em></p>\n<h3>SliderContext &#x26; useSliderContext()</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>SliderContext</code></strong>: React context providing slider state and methods:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>step</code>, <code>values</code>, <code>orientation</code>, <code>rtl</code></li>\n<li><code>trackRef</code> -- Ref to track element.</li>\n<li><code>setValueAt(index, value)</code> -- Updates value for a specific thumb.</li>\n<li><code>positionToValue(pos, rect)</code> -- Converts pointer position to slider value.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>useSliderContext()</code></strong>: Hook for accessing <code>SliderContext</code>. Throws an error if used outside <code>SliderPrimitive.Root</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul></componentpreview></componentpreview>",
