    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-1\" description=\"A toggle component.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Toggles represent a stateful action -- not navigation, not form submission, but \"turn this on or off.\" The distinction from buttons matters: toggles carry <code>aria-pressed</code> state and communicate their current value visually. We integrate with <code>@gentleduck/variants</code> to keep visual states clean and type-safe.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD   Toggle[Toggle]   Toggle --> variants[\"@gentleduck/variants\"]:::internal   Toggle --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal   variants --> |\"provides\"| VariantSystem[\"Variant System\\n(default, outline)\"]   variants --> |\"provides\"| Sizes[\"Size Variants\\n(sm, default, lg)\"]   Toggle --> |\"wraps\"| NativeInput[\"Native Checkbox\\n(hidden input)\"]   Toggle --> |\"manages\"| AriaPressed[\"aria-pressed\\nState\"]   classDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add toggle\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install the following dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/variants @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Add the <code>Toggle</code> component to your project.</step></p>\n<p>The <code>ToggleGroup</code> component uses the <a href=\"/components/toggle\"><code>Toggle</code></a> component. Make sure you have it installed in your project.</p>\n<p><step>Copy and paste the following code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"toggle\">\n<p><step>Update the import paths to match your project setup.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Toggle } from '@/components/ui/toggle'\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Toggle>Toggle&#x3C;/Toggle>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Default</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-2\" description=\"A toggle component.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>Outline</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-3\" description=\"A toggle component using the outline variant.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>With Text</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-4\" description=\"A toggle component with text.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>Small</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-5\" description=\"A small toggle component.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>Large</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-6\" description=\"A large toggle component.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h3>Disabled</h3>\n<p><componentpreview name=\"toggle-7\" description=\"A disabled toggle component.\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Toggle</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>(required)</td><td>The value associated with the toggle input</td></tr><tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td><code>'default' | 'outline'</code></td><td><code>'default'</code></td><td>Visual style variant of the toggle</td></tr><tr><td><code>size</code></td><td><code>'default' | 'sm' | 'lg'</code></td><td><code>'default'</code></td><td>Size variant of the toggle</td></tr><tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Disables the toggle if set to <code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Content rendered inside the toggle label</td></tr><tr><td><code>ref</code></td><td><code>React.Ref&#x3C;HTMLInputElement></code></td><td>--</td><td>Ref forwarded to the underlying hidden input element</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>input</code> props (via <code>Omit&#x3C;React.HTMLProps&#x3C;HTMLInputElement>, 'size'></code>).</em></p>",
