    "content": "<p><componentpreview name=\"tooltip-1\" description=\"tooltip\"></componentpreview></p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Floating UI powered positioning</strong> - Smart placement with <code>flip</code>, <code>shift</code>, and <code>offset</code> middleware.</li>\n<li><strong>State-aware styling hooks</strong> - <code>data-open</code> and <code>data-side</code> attributes for open state and placement styling.</li>\n<li><strong>Transform-origin variable</strong> - Uses <code>--duck-tooltip-content-transform-origin</code> for direction-aware animations.</li>\n<li><strong>Customizable delays</strong> - Control open/close delays with <code>delayDuration</code> and <code>skipDelayDuration</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Flexible triggers</strong> - Wrap any element using <code>asChild</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Accessible by default</strong> - Implements proper ARIA attributes and keyboard navigation.</li>\n<li><strong>Portal rendering</strong> - Renders tooltips in a portal to avoid layout clipping.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Tooltips are the lightest touch of contextual help -- they appear on hover, require no interaction, and disappear when attention moves on. We build on Floating UI because positioning against viewport edges, scroll containers, and dynamic layouts is harder than it looks. The <code>data-open</code> and <code>data-side</code> attributes give you animation hooks without JavaScript state management.</p>\n<h2>How It's Built</h2>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={`graph TD\nTooltip[Tooltip]\nTooltip --> primitives[\"@gentleduck/primitives\\n/tooltip\"]:::internal\nTooltip --> motion[\"@gentleduck/motion\"]:::internal\nTooltip --> libs[\"@gentleduck/libs\"]:::internal</p>\n<p>primitives --> |\"uses\"| floatingUI[\"Floating UI\"]:::external\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| Positioning[\"Smart Positioning\\n(flip, shift, offset)\"]\nprimitives --> |\"provides\"| A11y[\"ARIA Attributes\"]\nmotion --> |\"provides\"| AnimVariants[\"Direction-aware\\nAnimations\"]\nTooltip --> |\"exposes\"| DataAttrs[\"data-open\\ndata-side\\nCSS hooks\"]</p>\n<p>classDef external fill:#818cf8,stroke:#6366f1,color:#fff\nclassDef internal fill:#2dd4bf,stroke:#14b8a6,color:#fff\n`} /></p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<tabs defaultvalue=\"cli\">\n<tabslist>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"cli\">CLI</tabstrigger>\n  <tabstrigger value=\"manual\">Manual</tabstrigger>\n</tabslist>\n<tabscontent value=\"cli\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @gentleduck/cli add tooltip\n</code></pre>\n</tabscontent>\n<tabscontent value=\"manual\">\n<steps>\n<p><step>Install dependencies:</step></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/primitives @gentleduck/motion @gentleduck/variants @gentleduck/libs\n</code></pre>\n<p><step>Copy the <code>Tooltip</code> component code into your project.</step></p>\n<componentsource name=\"tooltip\">\n<p><step>Ensure import paths match your project structure.</step></p>\n</componentsource></steps>\n</tabscontent>\n</tabs>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { Tooltip, TooltipContent, TooltipTrigger } from '@/components/ui/tooltip'\n\n&#x3C;Tooltip delayDuration={500} skipDelayDuration={100}>\n  &#x3C;TooltipTrigger>Hover&#x3C;/TooltipTrigger>\n  &#x3C;TooltipContent>Tooltip text&#x3C;/TooltipContent>\n&#x3C;/Tooltip>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<h3>Custom Trigger with <code>asChild</code></h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Tooltip>\n  &#x3C;TooltipTrigger asChild>\n    &#x3C;span className=\"cursor-pointer underline\">Hover me&#x3C;/span>\n  &#x3C;/TooltipTrigger>\n  &#x3C;TooltipContent>Custom element trigger&#x3C;/TooltipContent>\n&#x3C;/Tooltip>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Animated Tooltip</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">&#x3C;Tooltip>\n  &#x3C;TooltipTrigger>Hover&#x3C;/TooltipTrigger>\n  &#x3C;TooltipContent className=\"TooltipContent\">Animated tooltip&#x3C;/TooltipContent>\n&#x3C;/Tooltip>\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-css\">.TooltipContent {\n  transform-origin: var(--duck-tooltip-content-transform-origin);\n  transition: transform 150ms ease, opacity 150ms ease;\n}\n\n.TooltipContent[data-open='false'] {\n  opacity: 0;\n  transform: scale(0.95);\n}\n\n.TooltipContent[data-open='true'] {\n  opacity: 1;\n  transform: scale(1);\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Styling Hooks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>data-open</code></strong> - Set on trigger and content (<code>true</code>/<code>false</code>) for state-based styling.</li>\n<li><strong><code>data-side</code></strong> - Set on content (<code>top</code>, <code>right</code>, <code>bottom</code>, <code>left</code>) for placement-aware styles.</li>\n<li><strong><code>--duck-tooltip-content-transform-origin</code></strong> - CSS variable for animation transform origin.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>API Reference</h2>\n<h3>Tooltip</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Tooltip sub-components (<code>TooltipTrigger</code>, <code>TooltipContent</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>placement</code></td><td><code>Placement</code></td><td><code>'top'</code></td><td>Tooltip placement relative to the trigger</td></tr><tr><td><code>open</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td>--</td><td>Controlled open state</td></tr><tr><td><code>defaultOpen</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td>--</td><td>Uncontrolled initial open state</td></tr><tr><td><code>onOpenChange</code></td><td><code>(open: boolean) => void</code></td><td>--</td><td>Callback when open state changes</td></tr><tr><td><code>delayDuration</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td>--</td><td>Milliseconds delay before showing or hiding the tooltip</td></tr><tr><td><code>skipDelayDuration</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td>--</td><td>Rest time in ms before opening when the pointer stops moving</td></tr><tr><td><code>sideOffset</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td>--</td><td>Offset along the main axis</td></tr><tr><td><code>alignOffset</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td>--</td><td>Offset along the cross axis</td></tr><tr><td><code>mainAxis</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td>--</td><td>Enables main-axis flipping while positioning</td></tr><tr><td><code>modal</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td>--</td><td>Enables focus management for the tooltip content</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all <code>TooltipPrimitive.Root</code> props (via <code>React.ComponentPropsWithRef&#x3C;typeof TooltipPrimitive.Root></code>).</em></p>\n<h3>TooltipTrigger</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>asChild</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Renders the child element as the trigger instead of a <code>button</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Content rendered inside the trigger</td></tr><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names to apply</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML button props (via <code>Omit&#x3C;React.ComponentPropsWithRef&#x3C;typeof TooltipPrimitive.Trigger>, 'size'></code>).</em></p>\n<h3>TooltipContent</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>className</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>--</td><td>Additional CSS class names to apply</td></tr><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Content rendered inside the tooltip</td></tr><tr><td><code>ref</code></td><td><code>React.Ref&#x3C;HTMLDivElement></code></td><td>--</td><td>Ref forwarded to the content container</td></tr><tr><td><code>forceMount</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Keep the content mounted for CSS-driven animations</td></tr><tr><td><code>renderOnce</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Render content only once and reuse the DOM node</td></tr><tr><td><code>lockScroll</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Locks scroll while the tooltip is open</td></tr><tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Disables focus management when true</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Also accepts all standard HTML <code>div</code> props (via <code>React.ComponentPropsWithRef&#x3C;typeof TooltipPrimitive.Content></code>).</em></p>\n<h3>TooltipPortal</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>children</code></td><td><code>React.ReactNode</code></td><td>--</td><td>Content to render inside the portal</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><em>Renders children into a React portal to avoid layout clipping.</em></p>",
