    "content": "<p>&#x3C;Callout icon={<zap>}></zap></p>\n<p>This package provides a collection of reusable React hooks for the <strong>@gentleduck/ui</strong> component library.</p>\n\n<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Hooks are the glue between React's render cycle and the real world -- browser APIs, external state, user interactions. Rather than scattering custom hooks across components, duck-hooks centralizes them as tested, typed utilities. Each hook solves one problem (media queries, local storage, intersection observer) and composes with others.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/hooks\n</code></pre>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>graph TD     A[duck-hooks] --> B[Ref Hooks]     A --> C[Timing Hooks]     A --> D[Layout Hooks]     A --> E[State Hooks]     B --> F[use-composed-refs]     C --> G[use-computed-timeout-transition]     C --> H[use-debounce]     D --> I[use-is-mobile]     D --> J[use-media-query]     E --> K[use-on-open-change]     E --> L[use-stable-id] </code>} /></p>\n<h2>Available Hooks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>use-composed-refs</code> -- Merge multiple refs into a single ref.</li>\n<li><code>use-computed-timeout-transition</code> -- Manage timeout-based transitions.</li>\n<li><code>use-debounce</code> -- Debounce a value.</li>\n<li><code>use-is-mobile</code> -- Detect if the user is on a mobile device.</li>\n<li><code>use-media-query</code> -- Use media queries in your components.</li>\n<li><code>use-on-open-change</code> -- Handle open/close state changes.</li>\n<li><code>use-stable-id</code> -- Generate a stable ID.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<p>To use a hook, import it from the corresponding directory:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import { useDebounce } from '@gentleduck/libs/use-debounce';\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const [value, setValue] = useState('');\n  const debouncedValue = useDebounce(value, 500);\n\n  return &#x3C;div>{debouncedValue}&#x3C;/div>;\n}\n</code></pre>",
