    "content": "<h2>Philosophy</h2>\n<p>Keyboard-driven interfaces aren't just for Vim enthusiasts -- they're an accessibility and power-user feature. duck-vim provides a registry-based key binding system where shortcuts are declared, not hardcoded. This means keybindings can be discovered (via the command palette), customized (per user), and composed (chord sequences) without touching component code.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Core is DOM‑only and framework‑agnostic.</li>\n<li>Optional React bindings provide a provider + hook for ergonomic usage.</li>\n<li>Supports multi‑step sequences with timeout and prefix matching.</li>\n<li>Written in TypeScript and ships types.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @gentleduck/vim\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-ts\">// Core\nimport { Registry, KeyHandler, type Command } from '@gentleduck/vim/command'\n\n// React bindings\nimport { KeyProvider, useKeyCommands } from '@gentleduck/vim/react'\n</code></pre>\n<p>If you're consuming from source inside a monorepo, import via your workspace alias or relative path.</p>\n<h2>Quick start - vanilla</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-ts\">import { Registry, KeyHandler, type Command } from '@gentleduck/vim/command'\n\nconst registry = new Registry(true)\nconst handler = new KeyHandler(registry, 600)\n\nconst openPalette: Command = {\n  name: 'Open Command Palette',\n  execute: () => console.log('palette!'),\n}\n\nregistry.register('ctrl+k', openPalette)\nregistry.register('g+d', { name: 'Go Dashboard', execute: () => console.log('dash') })\n\nhandler.attach(document)\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Quick start - React</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-tsx\">import React from 'react'\nimport { KeyProvider, useKeyCommands } from '@gentleduck/vim/react'\n\nfunction App() {\n  useKeyCommands({\n    'g+d': { name: 'Go Dashboard', execute: () => console.log('dash') },\n    'ctrl+k': { name: 'Open Palette', execute: () => console.log('palette') },\n  })\n\n  return &#x3C;div>Press g then d, or Ctrl+K&#x3C;/div>\n}\n\nexport default function Root() {\n  return (\n    &#x3C;KeyProvider debug timeoutMs={600}>\n      &#x3C;App />\n    &#x3C;/KeyProvider>\n  )\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Concepts</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Key descriptor</strong> - <code>ctrl?+alt?+meta?+shift?+key</code> (lowercased). Aliases: <code> </code> → <code>space</code>, <code>escape</code> → <code>esc</code>, <code>control</code> → <code>ctrl</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Sequence</strong> - steps joined by <code>+</code>, e.g. <code>g+d</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Prefixes</strong> - registering <code>g+d</code> marks <code>g</code> as a prefix while awaiting the next key.</li>\n<li><strong>Timeout</strong> - an active prefix expires after <code>timeoutMs</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&#x3C;MermaidDiagram chart={<code>flowchart LR     A[User Input] --> B[KeyHandler]     B --> C[Registry]     C --> D{Match?}     D -->|Yes| E[Execute Command]     D -->|No| F[Buffer / Discard]     G[React Hook] -.-> C </code>} /></p>\n<h2>API (core)</h2>\n<h3><code>Command</code> type</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-ts\">interface Command {\n  name: string\n  description?: string\n  execute: &#x3C;T>(args?: T) => void | Promise&#x3C;void>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Registry</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Signature</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>constructor</code></td><td><code>(debug?: boolean)</code></td><td>Create a new registry, optionally enabling debug logging</td></tr><tr><td><code>register</code></td><td><code>(key: string, cmd: Command)</code></td><td>Register a command for a key sequence</td></tr><tr><td><code>hasCommand</code></td><td><code>(key: string): boolean</code></td><td>Check if a command is registered for a key</td></tr><tr><td><code>getCommand</code></td><td><code>(key: string): Command | undefined</code></td><td>Retrieve the command for a key</td></tr><tr><td><code>isPrefix</code></td><td><code>(key: string): boolean</code></td><td>Check if a key is a prefix of a registered sequence</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>KeyHandler</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Signature</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>constructor</code></td><td><code>(registry: Registry, timeoutMs = 600)</code></td><td>Create a handler bound to a registry with a sequence timeout</td></tr><tr><td><code>attach</code></td><td><code>(target = document)</code></td><td>Start listening for keyboard events on the target</td></tr><tr><td><code>detach</code></td><td><code>(target = document)</code></td><td>Stop listening for keyboard events on the target</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Behavior:</strong> ignores pure modifier keys; attempts full-sequence match, waits on prefix, retries last key, then resets.</p>\n<h2>React bindings</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th>Export</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>KeyProvider</code></td><td>Mounts <code>Registry</code> + <code>KeyHandler</code>, attaches on mount</td></tr><tr><td><code>useKeyCommands(commands)</code></td><td>Registers mappings under the provider</td></tr><tr><td><code>KeyContext</code></td><td>Advanced access to <code>{ registry, handler }</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Advanced usage &#x26; tips</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Attach handlers to specific elements for scoped shortcuts.</li>\n<li>Create multiple registries for isolation between features.</li>\n<li>Call <code>registry.getCommand('...')?.execute()</code> for programmatic triggers.</li>\n<li>Enable <code>debug</code> during development to log matching behaviour.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&#x3C;Callout icon={<zap>}></zap></p>\n<p><strong>You can make your own binding to your own Framework, hence this package is framework-agnostic.</strong></p>\n",
